## Network Jobs

Local skill suite for warm-intro job search. All data is on this machine under `~/.network-jobs/`.

Skills are self-describing, so agents normally route on their own. This snippet is only
useful if you want to pin the workflow explicitly in a project's instructions.

### Routing

| User intent | Skill |
|-------------|-------|
| First install / résumé → profile / preferences interview | `network-jobs-setup` |
| Import a LinkedIn connections export | `network-jobs-import` |
| Find career pages + stage open roles | `careers-discover` |
| Promote triage → searchable corpus | `jobs-ingest` |
| Search openings in my network | `network-jobs` |
| Draft a forwardable warm intro | `intro-email-generator` |

### Rules

- There is no hosted API. Read only local files under `~/.network-jobs/`.
- Never invent job fields (salary, dates) that were not captured.
- Any "pick from these options" step uses the host's choice tool (`AskUserQuestion`,
  `question`, `ask_user_choice`, or equivalent): **one question per call, wait for
  the answer, then ask the next** — never a bundled prompt or multi-question call.
  Lead with your recommendation and a one-line reason, put the deciding data in the
  option labels, and keep a free-text/"none of these" path. Only fall back to a
  short numbered list (recommendation first, max 4) when the host has no such tool.
- `careers-discover` stages only; wait for user confirmation before `jobs-ingest`.
- Prefer `agent-browser` for JS-heavy career sites; fall back to curl/WebFetch.
- Helpers ship inside each skill folder (`helpers/`); suite root is in `~/.network-jobs/suite-root`.
